  "name": "pause-queues-and-expires",
  "description": "While px-b is paused it accepts and forwards no new marker: an arriving marker is queued and can only wait or expire. req-expires-in-queue arrives at step 2, is queued, and its TTL runs out before resume at step 5, so it is dropped with the specific reason expired_while_paused -- the queue never turns an expiry into a late delivery. req-arrives-on-resume reaches px-b in the very step the resume takes effect and is forwarded normally. The plan minimises total paused-proxy steps first, so the pause is only as long as the drain requires.",
